From 065cb71cda5e3f7d7da6623f8f345808df018543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:34:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: HDMI VRR off by default, on by itself for a
 video at its own rate

NVKMS turns HDMI VRR on in every mode of 50 Hz and up on a display that
declares it, and some TVs go to their game mode while it is on: a user
with an RTX 5090 had to add nvidia_modeset.conceal_vrr_caps=1 to keep
his TV out of it for films. Kodi has no use for VRR in the menus or for
a video at the fixed refresh of its mode, Dolby Vision leaves it off
already, and amdgpu and i915 give the desktop no HDMI VRR.
"HDMI variable refresh rate (VRR)" is off by default now: every mode set
that Kodi makes asks for VRR off where nvidia-drm offers
NV_HDMI_VRR_OFF. On, it is left to the driver, as before.

"Video at its own rate with VRR" needs VRR in the mode of the menus. It
stays one switch: while it is on, the mode sets leave VRR to the driver
too (CHdmiVrrOff::Allowed()). A mode of the menus that was set with VRR
off keeps a fixed refresh whatever the flips ask for, so a video is not
played at its own rate in it: Decide() says why, and Kodi goes on as
before until the next change of mode, which allows VRR.

The help of the setting says that some TVs go to their game mode with
VRR, that it is off by default, and that "Video at its own rate with
VRR" turns it on by itself.
